      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the areas of both the square and the circle, and then determine the difference between these areas.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the side length of the square.**\n\nThe diagonal of a square with side length \\( s \\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\ns\\sqrt{2} = 5\n\\]\nSolving for \\( s \\):\n\\[\ns = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the area of the square.**\n\nThe area \\( A_{\\text{square}} \\) of the square is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{square}} = s^2 = \\left( \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right)^2 = \\frac{25 \\cdot 2}{4} = \\frac{50}{4} = 12.5 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the radius of the circle.**\n\nThe diameter of the circle is 5 inches, so the radius \\( r \\) is:\n\\[\nr = \\frac{5}{2} = 2.5 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the area of the circle.**\n\nThe area \\( A_{\\text{circle}} \\) of the circle is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{circle}} = \\pi r^2 = \\pi (2.5)^2 = \\pi \\cdot 6.25 = 6.25\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\n**Step 5: Calculate the difference in areas.**\n\nThe difference in area between the circle and the square is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{circle}} - A_{\\text{square}} = 6.25\\pi - 12.5\n\\]\nUsing the approximation \\(\\pi \\approx 3.14159\\):\n\\[\n6.25\\pi \\approx 6.25 \\times 3.14159 \\approx 19.6349375\n\\]\nThus, the difference is:\n\\[\n19.6349375 - 12.5 \\approx 7.1349375 \\approx 7.1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the circle is greater than the area of the square by \\(\\boxed{7.1}\\) square inches.",
